WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.950
- As it seems to happen every few months,

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.870
certain politicians are making a big stink

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.810
about section 230 of the
Communications Decency Act.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.670
The funny thing is, that
if they were successful

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.940
in repealing section 230,

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.130
it would be disastrous
for those politicians

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.190
because it does two things.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.620
Number one, it allows
platforms to moderate.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.460
And number two, it provides a shield

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.610
so that if a user posts something,

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.330
the platform isn't
responsible for that post.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:24.720
And while a lot of people
are mad about the moderation,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.460
If that shield was destroyed,
a lot of those accounts,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.900
the ones that are at risk,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.410
that are peddling conspiracy theories

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.680
and are possibly defamatory,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.250
would be simply shut down.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:34.610
The first one to be shut down?

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.310
Probably President Trump's.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:39.000
So as the old proverb says,
be careful what you wish for.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.090
I did a whole video on this
in the past, check it out.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:41.950
And if you liked this video,

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.310
check out my other Eagle Briefs

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:44.851
where I cover the legal issues of the day.

00:00:44.851 --> 00:00:47.153
And as always, I'll see you in court.

